{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/778911-invictus-knight-order-initiation","id":778911,"title":"Invictus knight order initiation.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T04:29:22-08:00","id":778911,"title":"Invictus knight order initiation.","content":"Hi everyone, I'm running a vampire game set in Paris at the moment and one of my players made an Invictus knight of the order of the Blackened Chalice. We were talking about the character and the oaths she would have to have taken as a part of becoming a member of the order of the Blackened Chalice so I decided to write up what her initiation into the order might have been like and I wanted to share it here.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The lights are dimmed and curtains pulled, sunset has just begun outside. A woman rests on one knee, clothed in silvered robes, her face shadowed by the cowl. 5 men wearing black robes stand in a crescent before her and the pedestal between them, the centre one holding a blackened chalice with a cracked rim and gaps where precious gems were pried out long ago.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The one with the chalice speaks &quot;Lady Emilie Bellerose, supplicant of The Order of the Black Chalice. You stand here this night to take the oaths of office of our order. Do you wish to proceed?&quot; the woman's hood falls further over her face as she nods slightly &quot;The first of our oaths, we swear to uphold our Prince's laws, for without law, we are nothing. Do you swear this oath, Lady Emilie Bellerose?&quot; &quot;I do so swear it&quot; The man places the chalice on the pedestal sitting before the woman. He then reaches under his robes and pulls a weathered sword long-sword from its scabbard and with quicksilver blur opens his palm and bleeds into the chalice then steps back to his place in the centre of the five. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The man to his left steps forward &quot;The second of our oaths, we swear to defend the Invictus in all our deeds, for the first estate is our power and our society. Do you swear this oath, Lady Emilie Bellerose?&quot; &quot;I do so swear it&quot; The man pulls out his own blade, a Japanese katana barely a foot in length and slashes it across his palm as well and bleeds heavily into the chalice before stepping back to his place. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The man second from the right steps forwards. &quot;The third of our oaths, we swear to treat all with respect whether they be kindred, ghoul or mortal, for respecting others is needed to respect oneself. Do you swear this oath, Lady Emilie Bellerose?&quot; &quot;I do so swear it&quot; The third man pulls out an ornamental knife with a dragon for a hilt, its eyes a pair of rubies that reflect a flame that doesn't exist. He slices his palm, grunting slightly from the pain, pouring the blood into the chalice, bringing it half full before he steps back to his place. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The man on the far left steps forwards, metal clanking underneath his robes as he does, the sword at his waist distorting the shape of his robes. &quot;The fourth of our oaths, we swear to act with honour in all things, for honour is a knight\u2019s armour and sword in the darkest of times. Do you swear this oath, Lady Emilie Bellerose?&quot; &quot;I do so swear it.&quot; The man pulls out a gleaming bastard sword, nearly his height in length and carelessly cuts his palm with it, revealing the bone under the flesh. He holds his palm over the chalice so the heavy flow of blood can enter it. The chalice is now very nearly full.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The fifth man steps forwards, moving with more care and hesitance than the others &quot;The fifth and most sacred of our oaths, we swear no to suffer the stain of amaranth on ourselves, for though we have our beasts, our souls must be inviolate. Do you swear this oath, Lady Emilie Bellerose?&quot; &quot;I do so swear it.&quot; The woman is visibly trembling now. The man slowly reaches for his hip and pulls forth a simple dagger, no longer than the length of his hand and pauses with the blade pressed against his palm, watching the woman kneeling before him, before he slowly drags it across his hand and squeezes out a scarce few drops into the chalice, filling it to the brim. He steps back into his place alongside the others, all of them holding their blade unsheathed in one hand with their other hand facing the chalice, their wounds still fresh, though none of them bleed. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The man in the centre speaks again &quot;You knelt here before us Lady Emilie Bellerose of the First Estate. Now you rise as Dame Knight Emilie Bellerose of the Order of the Black Chalice.&quot; The woman stands and pushes her hood back, before pulling her own blade out from under her robes, a fine ornamental longsword that shines as if it were forged the previous night. Stepping forward she opens her own palm and pours blood into the chalice, which quickly overflows. The blood runs down the edges of the once ornate cup onto its base, where they disappear before reaching the pedestal.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6365,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","user":"Fumus","date":". 12-03-2015, 07:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}